# Rollback commands

If the new image is unhealthy, restore the previous image tag:

```powershell
$rollbackTag = "2026-10-22-003"
```

Then run through SSM:

```powershell
$commands = @(
  'set -eu',
  "sed -i 's|540087632943.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/shiftweave:[^ ]*|540087632943.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/shiftweave:$rollbackTag|' /mnt/shiftweave/compose.yaml",
  'cd /mnt/shiftweave',
  'docker compose up -d app'
)

@{commands=$commands} |
  ConvertTo-Json -Compress |
  Set-Content -Path .\ssm-rollback.json -Encoding ascii

$commandId = aws ssm send-command `
  --instance-ids i-08e66aa7d1bdd0c6c `
  --document-name AWS-RunShellScript `
  --parameters file://ssm-rollback.json `
  --comment "Rollback ShiftWeave application image" `
  --region us-west-2 `
  --query "Command.CommandId" `
  --output text

Write-Host "CommandId: $commandId"

aws ssm wait command-executed `
  --command-id $commandId `
  --instance-id i-08e66aa7d1bdd0c6c `
  --region us-west-2

aws ssm get-command-invocation `
  --command-id $commandId `
  --instance-id i-08e66aa7d1bdd0c6c `
  --region us-west-2 `
  --query "{Status:Status,ResponseCode:ResponseCode,Output:StandardOutputContent,Error:StandardErrorContent}" `
  --output json

Remove-Item .\ssm-rollback.json -Force
```

The permanent workflow is:

```text
typecheck/build
→ ECR login
→ new ARM64 image tag
→ push to ECR
→ verify ECR tag
→ SQLite backup
→ pull image on EC2
→ update Compose
→ restart app only
→ verify container
→ verify readiness
→ verify health
→ verify MCP
```

Keep `DEMO_USER` and `DEMO_PASSWORD` until the public-access deployment is separately completed and verified.
